@startuml
title <Flow name>  ' e.g. Create appointment

' Core architecture participants (keep these; add others only if the flow uses them)
actor Client
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js)" as FE
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB
'participant "Worker (Procrastinate)" as Worker
'participant "Twilio" as SMS

Client -> FE : submit (e.g. booking form)
FE -> NGINX : POST /v1/<resource>          ' BO flows use /bo/v1/<resource>
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  AuthN: session cookie required
  AuthZ: role = client | staff | admin
end note
BE -> BE : <Serializer>.validate()
note right of BE
  Validations:
  - required fields ...
  - ...
end note
BE -> BE : services.<operation>()
note over BE
  Business rules (see business-rules.md):
  - ...
  - run inside atomic txn / lock where needed
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT ... (selectors.<fn>)
BE -> DB : INSERT/UPDATE ... (models)
'BE -> Worker : enqueue <task>
BE --> FE : <status> (serialized result)
FE --> Client : result UI
@enduml
